WEBVTT

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.520
Why?

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.270
This country is filled with the smiles of its people...

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:12.420
Why would you destroy it?

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.770
You should know why better than anyone,

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.190
Marie Ange.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.050
There exists no love in this world that lasts forever.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.370
All flames soon die out, leaving nothing but ash!

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.740
That... is not true!

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:36.850
Ange!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.810
Princess Ann...

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.940
<i>Why do I dream such dreams?</i>

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.650
<i>Why must I awaken with such sorrow in my heart?</i>

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:00.040
{OP}

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.250
Happy go lucky girls! Precure! Yeah!

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.710
The world is like a merry-go-round

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.580
Love makes it turn, 3, 2, 1

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.620
Every day it sparkles

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.280
Dokidoki Precure

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.190
I wear my new clothes and walk a path I've never walked before

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.880
My heart races and I greet the scenery around me

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.510
The color of the flower on the corner will be my lucky color for the day

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:40.950
Leave it all to me, because today I'm blessed

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:46.650
If your friends are in trouble

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:55.530
isn't it normal to help them?

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.190
Happy lucky Precure

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.590
Only Precure makes my heart pound

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.430
Our happy love will change the world

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:05.230
What's more than just cute

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:09.100
is our promise between girls

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:15.140
I will fight for you and believe in you

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:21.050
Gather your unparalleled tenderness, yeah, Precure

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.070
A Celebration With Everyone!

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.070
A Celebration With Everyone!

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.670
You are a Leo.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.540
Leo

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.540
 You are a Leo. You may end up arguing with your friends often, 
 but eating sweets with them may bring you closer together.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.540
You may end up arguing with your friends often,

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.670
but eating sweets with them may bring you closer together.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.280
Your lucky item is a teddy bear.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.460
Sounds cool!

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.420
Lance, it's your turn.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.420
I'm not a stuffed animal, you know.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.360
What are you doing?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.620
Horoscopes.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.470
You find your zodiac sign with your birthday

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:01.360
and learn your fortune and compatibility with others.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.050
I was born on August 4th, so I'm a Leo.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.040
Makopi was born on November 4th, so she's a Scorpio.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.380
Alice is a Gemini,

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.630
and Rikka's a Virgo!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.570
Rikka, you're not into it?

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:19.620
Well, there are a lot of people in the world with the same birthdays,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.710
so when you say that they'll all have the same fate...

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:24.290
Wait.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.920
Did they do horoscopes in Trump Kingdom?

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:28.960
We did.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.860
The princess loved them, in fact!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.400
I'm home!

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.110
Welcome back!

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.800
You seem to be having fun.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.310
Yes, we were just having fun with horoscopes.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.050
Hey, what's your sign, Aguri?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.380
I don't know.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.790
I'll look it up for you.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.270
When's your birthday?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.950
Like I said, I don't know.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:00.090
I'm aware that birthdays are celebrations where birthday cake is eaten,

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.660
but I've never eaten one myself.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.030
But not to worry!

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.990
Someone will invite me to their birthday party,

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:11.300
and when that day comes, I'll finally have my chance to savor the phantom treat!

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:16.170
That hope is what drives me forward.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.280
And now, I must bid you adieu.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.180
Bye bye!

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.650
Mana, a word?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.460
She's adopted?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:41.320
Yes. Aguri isn't Mari's real granddaughter. {Wait, this is news?}

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:46.040
From what I heard, Aguri had no relatives, so Mari took her in.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.930
Does Aguri know that?

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.340
Yes.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.270
They're not related by blood,

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.750
but they live as a true grandparent and grandchild would.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.350
So don't treat her any differently, okay?

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.290
We did something mean to Aguri...

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.940
Well, we didn't know.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.930
We didn't mean any harm.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.590
I don't believe Aguri minded much.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.200
I hope so...

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.920
Besides, why didn't Aguri ever tell us something that important? {Didn't she tell you she was born in the Trump Kingdom world like 15-20 episodes ago?}

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.940
Rachel's right!

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.010
Perhaps she left it unsaid <i>because</i> it was important.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.670
The truth is, I don't have parents either.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:37.450
I was told I lost them in an accident when I was still a baby.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.180
So I don't even remember what my mother and father looked like.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.200
But I wasn't sad.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.350
We were all supported by the princess's love. {Wait, how old is the princess, again?}

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.380
Really?

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:09.260
Why didn't you ever tell us something that important?!

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:13.830
I didn't want you worrying over nothing.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.900
I suppose even the closest of friends don't tell each other everything.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.610
Mana?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.980
What is it?

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:26.770
We gotta celebrate!

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.560
Huh?

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.580
We'll throw a birthday party for Aguri

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.710
and we'll all jump in and celebrate!

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:33.940
When?

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.540
Aguri said she didn't know her birthday.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:40.580
If she doesn't know, then we can just throw one whenever, right?

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.410
What kind of logic is that?

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.290
We'll have it tomorrow!

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.670
Get your presents ready and come on over!

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.430
But...

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.400
don't say a peep to Aguri about this!

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.070
Got it?

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:57.230
Yeah, got it.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:08.030
What's eatin' you? You look like a dead fish.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:15.090
<i>Because we came to this stage for you!</i>

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:19.970
<i>I know that deep down, your heart is pure.</i>

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:24.190
<i>And I know that it's brimming with love!</i>

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.130
<i>What's with those girls?</i>

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.990
<i>One look, and it's all love, hearts, and junk...</i>

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.100
I'm dead tired.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.350
Caught a cold?

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:36.710
No.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.530
Figured.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.010
Idiots don't get colds, right?

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.950
Who's the idiot here?

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.160
She has a point, Ira.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.510
If you blurt out everything with no tact,

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.190
girls will never like you.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.620
Hey! That's my pudding à la mode!

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.520
Oh, my apologies!

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.360
It was in the fridge, so I couldn't resist!

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.590
You'll pay with your life!

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:12.440
Ain't that a bit much for just one pudding?

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.590
You don't get <i>anything</i>.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:18.820
Sweets are magical treats that turns a girl's frown upside down!

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.800
Where ya goin'?

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.070
To the Human World.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:33.130
The only way to fill my empty belly is to steal all their sweets!

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.410
Have a nice triiii—

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.810
What, did I say you could stay?

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.240
Ow, ow, ow...

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.360
Lemme go, c'mon!

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:40.800
Ow, ow, ow...

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.700
Ange!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.480
That dream again...

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:57.920
Aguri...

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.120
Can't sleep?

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.550
Grandmother...

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.160
Thank you very much.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.500
Is something troubling you?

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.750
I've been having the same dream every night, so I can't stay asleep...

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.900
I've been having one too.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.980
It's one where you grow up.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.260
One where I grow up?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.780
You wear a white dress and makeup...

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.130
I'm certain it was your wedding dress.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:45.430
I'll never get married!

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.670
I'll stay with you forever!

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.770
So you say.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.640
But the time will come when you'll embark on the journey of life.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:56.790
That's just the star you were born under. {I hate to translate it so literally, but I assume this is supposed to tie into the horoscope thing earlier so shouganai}

00:09:58.600 --> 00:09:59.810
Grandmother...

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:02.840
Now, go back to bed.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.130
Um...

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:07.360
What is it?

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.690
Can I sleep in your bed tonight?

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.060
Still such a child.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:41.860
Sugar?

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:42.580
Check.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:43.370
Flour?

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:43.950
Check.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.220
Eggs, milk, and cream?

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.120
Check.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.120
Hello.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.100
Makoto, you're grocery shopping?

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:52.560
You're mistaken.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.440
I am not this "Kenzaki Makoto" of which you speak.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:57.600
Excuse us.

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.730
We really should go with roses, huh?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.780
But we're on a budget...

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:13.520
What are you discussing?

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.490
If you're shopping for gifts, I wouldn't mind helping you choose!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.160
Oh, we're fine!

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.620
But we're in a bit of a rush, so...

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.840
Thank you, I'm sure she'll be delighted.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:35.480
Now, please keep it a secret from Aguri...

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.510
I'm home!

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:39.610
Welcome home.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.920
What is this secret about?

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.120
Um...

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.300
Sebastian?

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:51.180
Madam was simply collecting shells by the sea, {ends on "shiteita tokoro" and I'm pointing this out because this is liberal as hell pun translation.}

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:53.970
but sadly ran out of storage for her massive spoils. {ends on "desukara"}

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:58.520
As such, we came to Ms. Madoka's residence to borrow a crate. {ends on"okarishiteita no desu"}

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.630
A crate for the sea, crate by the sea, crate sea, crate sea, crate...

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:02.500
Seacrate! {starts on "naimitsu." I'm quite proud of this masterpiece.}

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.280
Well now, have a nice day!

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.820
What <i>was</i> he talking about?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.830
I wonder that myself.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.290
Really, everyone has been acting strange today!

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:26.960
The second they see my face, they try to run and hide.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.030
Aguri.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:31.240
Would you like to eat out tonight?

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.780
Even though I just bought groceries?

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.650
I made some plans.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.870
Be at the Pig's Tail Diner by 6 tonight.

